# px-bench.ini example (Windows host)

Copy your production `px.ini` to `px-bench.ini` and change only what is needed for side-by-side A/B.

```ini
[proxy]
; Keep the same pac= / server= / auth / noproxy as production
port = 3129
; Ensure WSL can connect (match how 3128 is exposed)
listen = 0.0.0.0

[settings]
; Same threads/idle/socktimeout as production
log = 1
log_file = px-bench.log
; Optional: shorter interval when exercising HTTP PAC soft-reload
; proxyreload = 5
```

Start without touching the live process on 3128:

```text
px-new.exe --config=px-bench.ini --foreground --verbose
```
